Setting switchboard up: each step says what's done already, and does only what isn't.

1. Accounts
No accounts yet. Each is a Claude subscription, whose token claude setup-token makes, run while signed in to it: add the first.
Its id, for good: letters, digits, - and _, such as work: work
Its label, to show it by (Enter for work): Work
Paste work's token, from claude setup-token run while signed in to that subscription (it won't show): 
Added work.
Add another account? [y/N] y
Its id, for good: letters, digits, - and _, such as work: side
Its label, to show it by (Enter for side): Side
Paste side's token, from claude setup-token run while signed in to that subscription (it won't show): 
Added side.
Add another account? [y/N] 
Which account are the browser and the Claude apps signed into? It's the primary: Claude Code's own token is its, and the router leaves a share of its quota for the apps.
The primary, of work, side (Enter for work): 
The primary is work · Work.

2. Priming
Priming starts each account's 5-hour window on a schedule, so their resets are spread through your day rather than coming together. It's optional.
Your day, HH:MM-HH:MM, such as 08:00-23:00 (Enter to leave priming off): 08:00-23:00
Priming is on, over 08:00-23:00.

3. The service
Installed <root>/home/Library/LaunchAgents/io.github.leeovery.switchboard.plist: launchd starts the router now, at every login, and whenever it stops.
The router is up: healthy, pid 4242.

4. The claude link
Linked <root>/home/.local/share/switchboard/bin/claude to <root>/brew/bin/switchboard.
claude doesn't go through switchboard yet: <root>/home/.local/share/switchboard/bin isn't on PATH. Add this line to your shell's startup file, such as ~/.zshrc, after anything else there that changes PATH, so it stays ahead of <root>/claude-code/bin:
export PATH="$HOME/.local/share/switchboard/bin:$PATH"
Running setup again, in a new terminal, checks it.

5. The skill
Installed the skill, which tells Claude what switchboard does under claude: <root>/claude/skills/switchboard/SKILL.md

6. Usage
(every account's usage)
